    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d756">

                <pb facs="0902" n="808" sameAs="frus:frus1930v03/pg808"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.512352 Shipping/22</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Spanish Ambassador</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Padilla</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-02-09">February 9, 1929</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 79–11</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Your Excellency</hi>: The attention of His Majesty’s
                    Government has been called to the fact that in the List presented by the
                    Treasury Department of the United States of Nations granting an equivalent
                    exemption of foreign shipping in accordance with the provisions of the Revenue
                    Act of 1921<anchor n="1" xml:id="d756-f1"/> the name of Spain does not
                    appear.</p>
                <p>In order to remedy this oversight, I have the honor to enclose herewith the text
                    of a Rapport of the “Ministerio de Hacienda”<anchor n="2" xml:id="d756-f2"/>
                    containing the Spanish Legislation on the matter according to which Your
                    Excellency will be able to observe the way in which the Spanish Law exempts
                    foreign ships from the payment of income tax and, therefore, that according to
                    the system of reciprocity established by the American Revenue Act of 1921, the
                    Spanish ships ought not be compelled to pay taxes in the United States.</p>
                <p>I will be much obliged to Your Excellency for being good enough to forward to the
                    Treasury Department the enclosed Rapport for said purpose.</p>
                <p>Accept [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Alejandro Padilla</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
